module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.gate_discriminates_below_its_measurements_reproducibility

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data gate_discriminates_below_its_measurements_reproducibility: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "gate_discriminates_below_its_measurements_reproducibility" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a merge-blocking gate whose line sits INSIDE the run-to-run variance of the quantity it compares, so admission is decided by which machine the subject landed on rather than by the subject** (the threshold is real, the measurement is of the right quantity, the comparison is correct, and the verdict is still not a property of the thing being judged. Nothing in the mechanism is wrong; the RESOLUTION of the decision is finer than the REPRODUCIBILITY of its input. ",

    "**THE DISTINGUISHING TEST IS A DETERMINISTIC WORK MEASURE BESIDE THE CLOCK, AND WITHOUT ONE THE CLASS IS UNDECIDABLE.** A cost that differs between two runs is otherwise ambiguous between the subject changing and the machine changing. Where the instrument publishes a per-subject work count that is a function of the declared work alone, an identical count across two runs is EVIDENCE that the declared work did not move -- and it is evidence rather than proof, which matters enough to state. **THE COUNT IS A MANY-TO-ONE FUNCTION OF THE WORK, SO EQUAL OUTPUTS DO NOT ENTAIL EQUAL INPUTS**: two different declared works can evaluate to the same number of steps, and the two runs compared here are different trees, where nothing forces the subject's declaration to be textually identical. What an identical count DOES establish is bounded and still decisive for this class: the difference in cost is not explained by a difference in evaluated step count, so an account of the crossing that appeals to the subject doing more work is ruled out. That is the inference the class needs -- it removes the competing explanation rather than proving the subject's identity. **THE STRONGER CLAIM IS AVAILABLE AND IS A SEPARATE CHECK NOBODY HAS RUN HERE: compare the subject's declaration between the two trees.** Where that is done, identity is established rather than inferred; where it is not, the honest form is the bounded one above. ",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc 2026-09-04, floor runs 33833513693 (main, green) and 33832137832 (an unrelated pull request, refused). Two identities, from `required_floor_claim_cost.tsv` in both runs: `v2.test.emit.rust_logic_meet_join_emit.rust_logic_meet_emit_holds` at eval_steps 159355 both times, cpu 312ms PASS against cpu 508ms REFUSED; and `v2.test.emit.rust_produced_decl_emit.rust_produced_decl_name_discriminates` at eval_steps 169297 both times, cpu 418ms PASS against cpu 500ms REFUSED. BYTE-IDENTICAL DECLARED WORK, 1.63x and 1.20x ON THE CLOCK, opposite verdicts, against a 500ms line. ",

    "**THE CONTROL THAT SEPARATES THIS FROM ORDINARY HOST CONTENTION IS PART OF THE CLASS AND NOT AN OPTIONAL EXTRA.** A floor cost refusal very often names a witness while actually measuring a busy machine, and if the whole distribution had shifted, the pair above would be an artefact with nothing to repair. It had not: over 2168 rows present in BOTH runs with identical eval_steps, the MEDIAN cpu ratio is 1.00 -- the corpus did not get slower. Restricted to rows above 100ms so small-cost noise cannot inflate it (n=299): median 1.08, p90 1.28, p99 1.69, max 1.97. **THE CONTROL REPLICATES ON A SECOND, INDEPENDENT PAIR, AND THE REPLICATION IS WHAT MAKES IT A CONTROL RATHER THAN A MEASUREMENT.** A different pair of runs, a different day-part and a host reporting loadavg 45.70 gives 2169 identical-eval_steps rows at median 1.000, and above 100ms (n=299) median 1.097, p90 1.204, p99 1.429. Two pairs agreeing to two decimals on the centre is a far stronger statement than either alone, and it kills a class of proposed remedies outright: if host load were the cause, scheduling or isolation would fix it, and a median unmoved at loadavg 45.7 says nothing about the host will. **WHAT THE MEDIAN CANNOT SETTLE IS THE PART THAT CROSSES.** A distribution can hold its centre perfectly while its tail widens, and only the tail can cross a budget -- these very pairs show the tail is not flat. So the measured claim is exactly this and no more: THE CORPUS DID NOT SHIFT, REPLICATED ON TWO PAIRS, AND WHETHER THE TAIL SPREAD IS LOAD-DEPENDENT IS UNMEASURED. **AN INDEPENDENT 54-RUN SWEEP THEN SETTLED THE TAIL HALF, AND IT REVERSED THIS ROW'S AUTHOR THREE TIMES.** **MOVING A CLOCK'S LINE DOES NOT FIX A CLOCK** -- that is the finding, and it is a third thing that neither reducing the cost nor regrounding the line names. **THE LOAD-BEARING RESULT IS A DIRECT OBSERVATION AND DEPENDS ON NO NULL MODEL, SO IT IS STATED FIRST.** Each run's OWN median cpu, over roughly 3580 claims, is 1 or 2ms across the ENTIRE corpus; the worst run -- 39 budget crossings -- has a median of 4ms, and five of the seven runs with ten or more crossings have a median of 2ms, IDENTICAL to the runs that crossed zero times. The centre is flat to within a millisecond while the crossing count ranges from 0 to 39. **THE DISTURBANCE IS IN THE TAIL AND NOT IN THE CENTRE**, which converts this row's earlier caveat -- that a median cannot answer a tail question -- into a measured fact about this corpus, and would stand untouched if every inferential number below were withdrawn. **THE FIRST SWEEP OF THIS POPULATION WAS CONTAMINATED BY THE VERY CLASS THIS LEDGER ROSTERS, AND THE CORRECTION IS RECORDED HERE RATHER THAN QUIETLY APPLIED.** It pooled budget_interrupted rows with completed ones. An interrupted row carries a RIGHT-CENSORED LOWER BOUND, not a cost, and those bounds cluster just above the ceiling that stopped them BY CONSTRUCTION -- so reading them as measured costs manufactures straddlers out of the budget itself. It reported 63 straddlers; 28 survive on measured cost and 35 were manufactured. The worst of them, produced_decl_two_targets_render_own_order, was reported crossing at 21% and HAS NEVER BEEN MEASURED ABOVE 500ms -- 41 exact rows spanning 367 to 464, beside 11 censored bounds reading 501 to 526, which is a picture of the budget and not of a distribution. rust_produced_decl_name_discriminates falls from 10 of 54 to 4 OF 48 EXACT ROWS, 8% rather than 19%. THE STRADDLERS SURVIVE AND THE RATES DO NOT, which is the correct shape of the damage: censoring inflates a rate without inventing a member. **AND THE RECOGNITION RULE THAT GENERALISES IT IS NOT ABOUT BAD DATA, WHICH IS WHY IT IS EASY TO MISS: A POPULATION VALID AT ONE GRAIN WAS SPENT AT ANOTHER.** A right-censored row is a REAL observation of a REAL identity that genuinely reached the ceiling. It is fully admissible evidence for the MEMBERSHIP question -- did this identity ever cross -- and inadmissible for the MAGNITUDE question, because its value is a lower bound pinned against the ceiling by construction. The usual contamination story is that the data was wrong; here the data was RIGHT FOR ONE QUESTION and the analysis asked the other while holding valid evidence for the first. So the tell is never a suspicious-looking row, it is a population admitted at the grain it answers and then reused at a grain it does not. **A SECOND TELL SITS AT THE REVIEWING LAYER AND IS THE SAME ERROR ONE LEVEL UP.** This row's figures were ratified by a reviewer who challenged the PROVENANCE OF THE STATISTIC -- chosen before or after the pattern was seen -- and never asked what POPULATION the rates were computed over. Those two audits do not overlap at all: a chosen statistic and a contaminated population each produce a number that survives every check made on the other. So `the analysis was scrutinised` is not a claim that partitions, and a reviewer must name WHICH of the two they covered. The danger is specific -- running one audit thoroughly produces the felt sense of having audited, which is the state in which the other half is waved through. **AND THE DEEPER REASON THIS ROW LEADS WITH ITS OBSERVATIONS IS NOW STATABLE, HAVING BEEN ARRIVED AT THE HARD WAY: EACH LAYER OF INFERENCE BETWEEN AN OBSERVATION AND A CLAIM IS A SURFACE A LATER CORRECTION CAN LAND ON.** The ordering was adopted to defend against a post-hoc statistic and it absorbed an unrelated population contamination, because a direct observation of a run's own median has neither a null model NOR a population to corrupt. Leading with the fewest layers is not modesty; it is minimising the surface a retraction can reach. **WHAT SURVIVED THE CORRECTION IS EXACTLY WHAT NEVER DEPENDED ON THE CENSORED POPULATION, WHICH IS WHY THIS ROW LEADS WITH THE OBSERVATION AND NOT THE INFERENCE.** The flat median is untouched, since no censored row enters a run's own median; the severe band is still empty; the median straddler still sits 38% below the line. The time clustering came back STRONGER at p=0.0027, which earns a precise label and no more -- POST-HOC, ROBUST TO A POPULATION CORRECTION: the statistic was fixed before the correction and survived it on a subset of the same corpus, and cleaning removes rows without generating new ones, so it cannot restore the blindness pre-registration would have given. **AND THE VARIANCE ARGUMENT IS LED BY THE ONE FIGURE THAT NEEDS NO POPULATION AT ALL: NEAR-CONSTANT WORK AGAINST A 1.55x MEASURED COST SPREAD.** rust_produced_decl_name_discriminates takes three distinct eval_steps values across 54 runs and measures 346ms to 538ms of cpu, exact rows only, no bound among them. That is a VALIDITY argument rather than a RATE argument -- it says the quantity the gate compares is not a property of the subject -- and no correction to any denominator can touch it. A rate can be inflated by a contaminated population; a spread on identical work cannot. **THE LINE IS NOT MISCALIBRATED AND THE COST IS NOT THE SUBJECT.** Of 3574 identities with at least ten observations, 28 straddle the budget ON MEASURED COST, and NONE were excluded by the eval_steps gate -- every straddler varies at CONSTANT WORK, one of them spanning 346ms to 549ms for the same three step values, so there is nothing to optimise. No identity has a p75 above the line (the closest is 482 against 500) and the straddlers' medians sit a median 38% BELOW it, the closest 18% below: the line sits well above the population's mass and is reached only by tails. **AND THE PER-RUN CROSSING COUNT IS BIMODAL** -- 31 of 54 runs cross zero times while single runs cross 22, 25 and 39 -- which 28 independent tails cannot produce, so a CORRELATED PER-RUN CAUSE acts on the tail. **THE DRIFT RESULT IS REAL AND IS RECORDED WITH ITS PROVENANCE, BECAUSE A p-VALUE IS A STATEMENT ABOUT A PROCEDURE AND A PERMUTATION CONTROLS FOR THE SHUFFLE AND FOR NOTHING ABOUT HOW THE STATISTIC WAS CHOSEN.** Mean crossing timestamp +1.49h against a shuffled null of +1.08h, permutation over 20,000 shuffles, p=0.0027 recomputed on the exact-only crossing set, with the high-count runs in the newest third of 52. **THE STATISTIC WAS SELECTED AFTER THE CLUSTERING WAS SEEN, IN A RUN-ORDERED LISTING PRINTED TO TEST SOMETHING ELSE, AND IT IS NOT PRE-REGISTERED.** The family is FOUR tested statistics -- order position, timestamp, server concentration, and a discarded independence estimate -- of which two returned significant, out of an unbounded set nobody can enumerate; a reader may correct for four and cannot correct for the untried. Two facts cut the other way and neither is a rescue. The candidate FIELDS (loadavg, runner identity, time of day, concurrent job count) were named in writing before any was tested, by a second party who simultaneously predicted the OPPOSITE outcome. And the TIMESTAMP variant was specified in advance by that same challenger as a FALSIFICATION test of the ordering result -- so its specification has clean provenance and it was designed to break the finding rather than to confirm it. **WHAT IT CONTROLS FOR IS THE CHALLENGER'S CONFOUND, NOT THE PRODUCER'S SELECTION**: it is the same corpus in which the effect had already been seen, and a second test on one dataset is not independent evidence. A burst confound was raised and is dead: inter-run gaps are 1.9 minutes over the first 33 runs and 1.7 over the last 19, so DENSITY IS FLAT WHILE THE TAIL FATTENS, which disposes of concurrency more strongly than the timestamp test alone. **THE 18:08-20:12 WINDOW IS A MECHANISM CONSTRAINT AND NOT CORROBORATION.** It was found in the data, so the effect is inside it by construction and it must not be added to the p-value as a second finding; what it does contribute is scale -- whatever accumulates does so over roughly TWO HOURS, not over a night, which excludes most of what a reader reaches for on hearing 'later'. **PROVISIONING IS NOT THE REMEDY, AND HOST STATE RATHER THAN HOST IDENTITY IS DIRECTLY OBSERVED.** The seven high-count runs sit on seven DIFFERENT hosts across three servers, and two hosts carry both a high run and a clean one -- srv1-15 carries the corpus's worst run at 39 crossings AND a run at zero, srv3-01 carries 10, 4 and 0. **THAT NEGATIVE IS NOT ESTABLISHED RATHER THAN RULED OUT**, and the reason is what stops it being cited as exoneration: 52 runs across 38 distinct hosts leaves most hosts with a single run, so a real host effect would be nearly invisible to that design, and those two WITHIN-HOST mixed pairs are its only informative observations. **THE NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER IS A CAUSAL TEST ANYONE CAN EXECUTE WITHOUT CONSULTING THIS ROW'S AUTHOR, WHICH IS WHAT SEPARATES A TRIGGER FROM A WISH.** Pin two floor runs of the SAME unchanged tree to ONE host, at least 90 minutes apart within a single window, and compare their per-claim cpu at p99 over the claims whose eval_steps are identical between them. The drift claim predicts the later run's p99 ratio exceeds 1.2 while its MEDIAN ratio stays within 0.05 of 1.0. A later-run p99 ratio at or below 1.05 FALSIFIES it; a median ratio that moves with the p99 refutes the tail-only mechanism and indicts the host or the tree instead. Executing that requires pinning runs on live infrastructure and is the operator's to authorise, which is why this row lands as a correlational finding with a named mechanism and a specified experiment rather than waiting on one. A report of this class without that control is indistinguishable from a slow-machine anecdote. ",

    "**THE PROPERTY THAT MAKES IT WORSE THAN `SOME ROWS ARE CLOSE TO THE LINE`: THE EXPOSED POPULATION IS INVISIBLE TO INSPECTION OF ANY PASSING RUN.** On the green run, rows visibly above 450ms: ZERO. A reader auditing that artifact sees nothing near the line and correctly concludes, from what is in front of them, that there is no exposure. ",

    "**HOW MANY ROWS ARE ACTUALLY EXPOSED DEPENDS ENTIRELY ON WHICH QUANTILE OF THE INFLATION DISTRIBUTION IS APPLIED, AND THE COUNT MUST NEVER BE QUOTED WITHOUT IT.** Sweeping the same 299-row above-100ms population by the ratios measured on one cross-tree pair: at p90 (1.28) FOUR rows cross, lowest exposed 394ms; at p95 (1.36) EIGHT, lowest 376ms; at p99 (1.69) FORTY-FOUR, lowest 296ms; at the observed max (1.97) SEVENTY, lowest 256ms. ",

    "**AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW QUOTED THE p90 FIGURE ALONE -- `zero visible, four exposed` -- AND THAT UNDERSTATES BY AN ORDER OF MAGNITUDE.** The correction was forced by observation within the hour: four distinct identities crossed, and the fourth had a main cost of 312ms, rank 29 of 3605, needing 1.61x. That is not outside the measured distribution -- IT SITS AT QUANTILE 0.983 OF THE 299 RATIOS -- so the p90 threshold did not fail to predict a freak, it was simply the wrong quantile. **CROSSING IS A TAIL EVENT BY CONSTRUCTION, SO READING A CROSSING THRESHOLD OFF A CENTRAL QUANTILE IS A CATEGORY ERROR RATHER THAN A CONSERVATIVE ESTIMATE.** All four observed crossings have main costs at or above 312ms, which the p99 figure covers and the p90 figure does not. ",

    "**AND IT IS A THRESHOLD SWEEP OVER ONE MEASURED RATIO DISTRIBUTION FROM ONE CROSS-TREE PAIR, NOT AN ESTIMATE OF A POPULATION.** The defensible claim is conditional in all three respects -- at the observed p99 inflation, 44 of the 299 rows above 100ms would cross -- and stating it any other way lends the number a denominator it has not earned. THE FACT THAT THE SWEEP NAMED REAL MEMBERS IN RANK ORDER IS EXACTLY WHAT MAKES THE UNQUALIFIED FORM DANGEROUS: main carried only SIX rows at or above 380ms with nothing above 460, and the crossings were ranks 1, 2 and 5 of those six. A figure that identifies actual rows acquires credibility its sample size cannot support. ",
    "AND THE SMALLNESS OF THE CROSSING POPULATION IS PART OF THE ARGUMENT RATHER THAN A WEAKNESS. Only two rows in 3602 exceeded the line on the failing run. This is not a corpus that is broadly over budget; it is a corpus with a narrow bracket of rows whose true cost STRADDLES the line. NON-DETERMINISM AT THE GATE, NOT A COST PROBLEM -- and the remedies differ completely: making the corpus faster does not fix a gate whose decision is a coin flip for whatever rows happen to sit in the bracket. ",

    "**A THIRD CROSSING, IN THE OTHER ARM, WITHIN AN HOUR OF THIS ROW BEING FILED -- AND IT IS ONE OF THE FOUR THE ESTIMATE SAID WERE INVISIBLE.** `v2.test.emit.produced_decl_two_target.produced_decl_two_targets_render_own_order` measured cpu 405ms and 409ms on two green runs at eval_steps 197227 in BOTH -- eighty-one percent of the line, nothing to see on any passing artifact -- and on run 33840355227 it was preempted at `cpu_at_least=502ms/500ms`, `raised_by=cpu_deadline`. The prediction confirmed itself on a row nobody would have flagged. ",

    "**AND IT IS THE WEAKEST OF THE THREE AS EVIDENCE, WHICH MUST BE SAID BESIDE IT: THREE CROSSINGS, TWO USABLE RATIOS.** This one landed in INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT, so its cost is RIGHT-CENSORED -- `cpu_at_least=502` is a lower bound and the true cost exceeds the line by an unbounded amount. IT MAY BE QUOTED AS A CROSSING AND NEVER AS A RATIO, and it must not be pooled with the two completed pairs when anyone computes an inflation figure, because a censored point admitted as a measurement inflates the estimate -- which is `right_censored_cost_read_as_exact` committed while reasoning about this row. The temptation to compute a percentile over `all three` is exactly what this sentence exists to stop. ",

    "**THE INTERRUPTED ARM IS ALSO WHERE THE CLASS BECOMES UNDIAGNOSABLE, WHICH IS WORSE THAN A SECOND INSTANCE.** A completed crossing yields a verdict and an exact figure, so it is legible as a crossing. An interrupt yields NO ANSWER AT ALL, so a genuine hang and a jitter crossing are indistinguishable there by construction -- and the remedy for both is the same rerun. That is the route by which a REAL hang is absorbed into the variance story and stops being investigated: not the gate deciding by machine, but the gate reaching an arm where its own diagnosis cannot be performed. ",

    "**THE HARM IS NOT ONLY THAT THE GATE DECIDES BY MACHINE -- IT IS THAT THE STANDARD REMEDY HIDES THE EVIDENCE THAT IT DID FROM EVERY INSTRUMENT ANYONE ACTUALLY READS.** A rerun is a new ATTEMPT on the same run id, not a new run. The failed attempt's conclusion is superseded by the successful one on the default and latest-attempt surfaces, so afterwards the run list shows a single clean row and the refusal survives in no field a reader consults except `run_attempt`. Every lane that meets a variance refusal, reruns, goes green and says nothing has converted a refusal into an admission that no ordinary reading will surface. AN EARLIER REVISION SAID THE EVIDENCE WAS ERASED, WHICH OVERSTATED IT: attempt-addressable evidence is retained at `runs/<id>/attempts/<n>`, so the honest claim is invisibility to the surfaces in use rather than destruction -- weaker, and true. The consequence for measurement is unchanged, because a population nobody can enumerate from the instruments they read is not measurable in practice. ",

    "**SO THE COUNT OF AFFECTED PULL REQUESTS CANNOT BE RECOVERED FROM HISTORY, AND ITS ABSENCE IS NOT EVIDENCE OF A SMALL POPULATION.** A reader asking how often this bites finds nothing, and finds nothing in the reassuring direction. IF RERUN-UNTIL-GREEN IS HOW LANES ROUTINELY GET PAST THIS GATE, THE GATE IS ALREADY NON-BLOCKING AND NOBODY HAS DECLARED IT -- a §4b(3) rung drop happening by practice rather than by declaration, which is precisely the state the declared-drop discipline exists to prevent. ",

    "**AND THE INSTRUMENT THAT WOULD DETECT IT INSTANTIATES THE CLASS BY DEFAULT.** A merge-readiness check counting runs on the head with a failing conclusion reads a rerun-green head as a first-attempt green: permanently green over exactly the population it was built to catch. That happened tonight -- a gate written in direct response to a disclosed rerun could not see that rerun until it was changed to read `run_attempt`, and it was written by the same author who had been told the rerun happened. THE ONLY FIELD THAT CARRIES THE FACT IS `run_attempt`, and nothing else in the record disagrees with a clean first pass. ",

    "**THE DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION FOLLOWS FROM THAT AND IS PART OF THE CLASS, NOT ETIQUETTE:** a green obtained by rerun must SAY SO in the artifact a merge decision reads, because the run record will not. Its first receipt is this row's own author, who reran gunbc#10327 to clear a refusal already shown to be machine variance, named the rerun as a non-discharge in the same breath, and still had to be asked to put it in the pull request body -- the honest reasoning lived in a message, and a message is not what a merge reads. ",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST THREE NEIGHBOURS. `artifact_declares_a_threshold_it_is_not_measured_against` is a threshold compared to the WRONG quantity; here the quantity is right. `right_censored_cost_read_as_exact` is a BOUND read as a point; here every figure is a completed measurement. And ordinary flakiness is a test whose OUTCOME is unstable; here the outcome is perfectly stable and the COST is not, so every green run looks deterministic and nothing in the subject is intermittent. ",

    "**TWO TRUE FINDINGS THAT DO NOT COMPOSE INTO A REMEDY, STATED HERE BECAUSE THE COMPOSITION IS THE OBVIOUS NEXT MOVE AND IT IS WRONG.** The same night this row was measured, the floor's opaque-host-call REACHABILITY column was repaired and became discriminating for the first time -- it had read `cooperatively_pollable` on 3602 of 3602 claims, a column that could not go the other way for any input, and now partitions 349 probed claims into 214 unbounded and 135 pollable with an empty intersection. Both findings are real and both concern the same claims, so the tempting inference is that the crossings are explained by reachability and that a reachability-conditioned budget would fix them. IT WOULD NOT. **A CLAIM THAT CROSSES BECAUSE THE HOST'S TAIL FATTENED OVER A TWO-HOUR WINDOW DOES NOT CROSS BECAUSE OF HOW IT POLLS**, and the arithmetic points the same way: the majority arm is the UNBOUNDED one, so a relaxation conditioned on reachability would apply to the minority. The reachability column answers what a claim can be interrupted at; this row answers why a clock-denominated line admits or refuses the same unchanged subject. Two instruments, two subjects, one corpus -- and the coincidence of corpus is the entire reason they will be composed by someone who reads only the numbers. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: FOR EVERY BLOCKING THRESHOLD, ASK WHAT THE SAME SUBJECT MEASURES ACROSS TWO RUNS, AND COMPARE THE SPREAD TO THE DISTANCE BETWEEN THE POPULATION AND THE LINE. If the p90 inflation moves any row across, that row's verdict is a fact about the machine. The tell available without a second run: a blocking line denominated in a CLOCK beside a published DETERMINISTIC work measure that nothing compares against. ",

    "**RUNG FOUND AT: BELOW THE LADDER, NOT MITIGATABLE, AND AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW SAID MITIGATABLE UNTIL REVIEW REFUSED IT (codex/gpt-5.6-sol, review 59774).** Rung 1 requires harm CONTAINED by total operations, typed outcomes, bounds, rollback or isolation. Nothing here contains anything: the gate emits a REFUSAL THAT IS NOT A PROPERTY OF THE SUBJECT, which is a fabricated verdict, and DESIGN section 4b places silent wrongness outside the ladder and forbids it outright. ",

    "**THE ONLY THING RESEMBLING A CONTAINMENT IS THE RERUN, AND THIS ROW ALREADY ESTABLISHES THAT THE RERUN IS THE SECOND HALF OF THE DEFECT.** It handles a jitter crossing and a genuine regression with the same gesture, it overwrites the failed attempt's conclusion, and it leaves no record that a verdict was reversed. Calling that containment would be citing the erasure mechanism as the mitigation -- and the inflation was written by the author of the paragraph immediately above that says so. ",

    "THE CORRECTION IS RECORDED RATHER THAN QUIETLY APPLIED, because rung inflation inside a row ABOUT INSTRUMENTS OVERSTATING THEMSELVES is the specimen the class most needs. A class that reaches the ladder only by ceasing to fabricate has not climbed a rung; it has become eligible to be ranked. ",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE, and honestly not higher. Wall-clock and CPU-clock costs on shared hardware are external facts, so no construction makes an unreproducible measurement reproducible -- DESIGN's OUTSIDE THE MODELED GUARANTEE column. What IS decidable is whether a gate is permitted to discriminate at a resolution its input cannot support. ",

    "**AN EARLIER REVISION NAMED A TRIGGER THAT WOULD HAVE DEFEATED THE SAFETY PURPOSE, AND THE CORRECTION IS RECORDED BECAUSE THAT IS THE EXACT DEFECT THE TRIGGER DISCIPLINE EXISTS TO CATCH.** It said: denominate the blocking decision in the deterministic work measure. That is wrong. THE SAFETY LIMIT EXISTS TO BOUND TIME, AND AN OPAQUE HOST CALL CONSUMES UNBOUNDED WALL TIME IN FEW EVALUATOR STEPS -- which is precisely the population this repository's preemption work is about. A step-denominated deadline would be blind to the one class it most needs to catch, so that trigger could have been satisfied in full while the capability it was meant to protect stayed dead. Section 4b retires a drop BY ITS TRIGGER AND BY NOTHING ELSE, which is what makes a plausible-but-wrong trigger worse than a missing one. ",

    "**SO THIS ROW'S FINDING IS ABOUT THE GATE'S REPEATABILITY AND DOES NOT LICENSE A REMEDY THAT TRADES AWAY THE TIME BOUND.** The two properties are independent: a decision can be reproducible and unsafe, or safe and unreproducible, and this row establishes only the second failure. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY AND WITH WHAT IT MUST BE SUFFICIENT FOR: A BLOCKING COST DECISION WHOSE VERDICT IS A FUNCTION OF THE SUBJECT RATHER THAN OF THE MACHINE, WHILE STILL BOUNDING TIME -- sufficient for two runs of an unchanged subject to reach the SAME verdict AND for an operation that consumes unbounded wall time in few evaluator steps to remain refusable. Both halves are required; a mechanism satisfying either alone leaves one of the two failures standing, and the first revision of this trigger satisfied only the first. ",

    "THREE THINGS THAT DO NOT DISCHARGE IT. Raising the line relocates the bracket without removing it and leaves the next row to straddle the new value. Rerunning until green is the absorbing fallback the ladder forbids, converting an unreproducible refusal into a silent admission. And denominating the decision in evaluator steps alone discharges the reproducibility half while removing the time bound, which is not a climb but a trade of one below-the-ladder failure for another.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
